ng Eggs - Learning to Read for Kids | Learn to Read with ...](https://readingeggs.com/)\n</tool_response>"},{"role":"assistant","content":"<think>\nThe search results are not all directly relevant. We have some PDFs, some Edutopia articles, and a few other resources. We need to open the most relevant ones: the \"Embracing a Holistic Approach to Supporting English Learner Students\" (pdf), \"Beyond Teaching English: Embracing a Holistic Approach to Supporting...\" (pdf). The \"Transformation of English Education in the Digital Era: A New Paradigm...\" (article). The \"Integrating Social and Emotional Learning in English Language Arts\" (Edutopia). \"Empowering Elementary Students With Disciplinary Literacy\" (Edutopia). \"Critical Literacy in Early Elementary Grades\" (Edutopia). \"Project-Based Learning for ELLs\" (Colorin Colorado). \"Foundations of Culturally and Linguistically Responsive Teaching\" (Edutopia). \"Whole-Child Approach to Education\" (Teaching Strategies blog). Also \"Transforming English Education in the Digital Era: A New Paradigm\" (maybe a research article). We can also search for \"holistic empowerment in English education PDF\" to get more.\n\nWe need to visit these pages to extract content. Let's start with the first PDF: \"Embracing a Holistic Approach to Supporting English Learner Students\" (https://files.eric.ed.gov/fulltext/EJ1206491.pdf). We'll use the visit tool to get a summary.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"visit\", \"arguments\": {\"url\": [\"https://files.eric.ed.gov/fulltext/EJ1206491.pdf\"], \"goal\": \"Summarize the key points, arguments, and recommendations about holistic approach to supporting English learner students.\"}}\n</tool_call>"},{"role":"user","content":"<tool_response>\nContent from https://files.eric.ed.gov/fulltext/EJ1206491.pdf:\n\n%PDF-1.5\r%����\r\n54 0 obj\r<\n>\rendobj\r \rxref\r54 50\r0000000016 00000 n\r\n0000001966 00000 n\r\n0000002065 00000 n\r\n0000002555 00000 n\r\n0000002850 00000 n\r\n000000