er students and their families, the\nmajority of whom are Latinx, through a multipronged approach that includes targeted academic instruction, the adoption of schoolwide\nvalues and behavioral expectations, a significant family-community outreach program, and teacher professional development in traumasensitive schooling and instruction. The authors share analyses and findings from data gathered through classroom and school event observations, separate focus groups of students and parents, interviews with key stakeholders, questionnaires from school personnel and parents, and publicly available school-level data. Implications for educators are shared with the goal of creating spaces and contexts where English learner students and their families succeed and indeed thrive.\n</tool_response>"}],"response":"<think>\nThe escholarship page is a PDF, but the content is not displayed. The visit tool only shows the top of the page. We need to get the PDF text. However, the PDF is large. We can try to use the \"download\" function? The visit tool can open the PDF and we can see the text. It may be too big. But we can try to request a specific part. Or we can search for a different source: \"holistic empowerment in English education PDF\". Let's search again with \"holistic empowerment in English education PDF\".\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"search\", \"arguments\": {\"query\": [\"\\\"holistic empowerment\\\" English education PDF\", \"\\\"holistic\\\" English language teaching\\\" PDF\", \"\\\"holistic\\\" English education\\\" research\\\"\"]}}\n</tool_call>","total_time_ms":2286.5428924560547,"rtt_ms":20.34584681193034,"inference_time_ms":2266.1970456441245}
