ture, family background, and home languages. Each project has the following sections:\n- the purpose of the project\n- materials suggested\n- questions for children\n- instruction to complete each section\n- additional activities and resources\nMost Popular10 Strategies for Building Relationships with ELLsUsing Cognates to Develop Comprehension in EnglishCulturally Responsive Instruction for Holiday and Religious CelebrationsLanguage Objectives: The Key to Effective Content Area Instruction for English Learners\n\n## Most Popular\n\n10 Strategies for Building Relationships with ELLsUsing Cognates to Develop Comprehension in EnglishCulturally Responsive Instruction for Holiday and Religious CelebrationsLanguage Objectives: The Key to Effective Content Area Instruction for English Learners\n10 Strategies for Building Relationships with ELLs\n10 Strategies for Building Relationships with ELLs\n\n### 10 Strategies for Building Relationships with ELLs\n\nUsing Cognates to Develop Comprehension in English\nUsing Cognates to Develop Comprehension in English\n\n### Using Cognates to Develop Comprehension in English\n\nCulturally Responsive Instruction for Holiday and Religious Celebrations\nCulturally Responsive Instruction for Holiday and Religious Celebrations\n\n### Culturally Responsive Instruction for Holiday and Religious Celebrations\n\nLanguage Objectives: The Key to Effective Content Area Instruction for English Learners\nLanguage Objectives: The Key to Effective Content Area Instruction for English Learners\n\n### Language Objectives: The Key to Effective Content Area Instruction for English Learners\n\nELL NewsCultivating Content and Language Learning in ELLsEdutopia| April 04, 2025See more headlines ›\n\n## ELL News\n\nCultivating Content and Language Learning in ELLsEdutopia| April 04, 2025\n- Cultivating Content and Language Learning in ELLsEdutopia| April 04, 2025\nEdutopia\n| April 04, 2025\nTweets by @ColorinColorado\n</tool_response>"},{"role":"assistant","content":"<think>\nThe PBL page is a list of resources, not a deep article. We also have \"Beyond Teaching English: Embracing a Holistic Approach to Supporting ...\". Let's open that.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"visit\", \"arguments\": {\"url\": [\"https://escholarship.org/uc/item/375574d9\"], \"goal\": \"Summarize the main points about holistic approach to supporting English learners.\"}}\n</tool_call>"},{"role":"user","content":"<tool_response>\nContent from https://escholarship.org/uc/item/375574d9:\n\n# Beyond Teaching English: Embracing a Holistic Approach to Supporting English Learner Students and Their Families\n\nDownloadPDFMainPDFShareEmailFacebook\nDownloadPDFMainPDFShareEmailFacebook\nDownloadPDFMainPDF\nMainPDF\n- MainPDF\n- PDF\nShare\nEmailFacebook\nEmailFacebook\n\n## Beyond Teaching English: Embracing a Holistic Approach to Supporting English Learner Students and Their Families\n\nBeyond Teaching English: Embracing a Holistic Approach to Supporting English Learner Students and Their Families\n2018Giboney Wall, Carrie R.;Musetti, Bernadette B.©2018by the author(s).Learn more.\n- Giboney Wall, Carrie R.;\n- Musetti, Bernadette B.\n©2018by the author(s).Learn more.\nPublished Web Locationhttps://doi.org/10.5070/B5.35950\nPublished Web Locationhttps://doi.org/10.5070/B5.35950\n\n## Published Web Location\n\n...Main ContentMetricsAuthor &ArticleInfoAbstractThis study describes the ways 1 elementary school is attempting to address the needs of its English learner students and their families, the\nmajority of whom are Latinx, through a multipronged approach that includes targeted academic instruction, the adoption of schoolwide\nvalues and behavioral expectations, a significant family-community outreach program, and teacher professional development in traumasensitive schooling and instruction. The authors share analyses and findings from data gathered through classroom and school event observations, separate focus groups of students and parents,